# Quality gates

Run all checks before opening a PR. CI enforces the same commands.
{% if platform in ('forgejo', 'both') %}
## CI secrets (Forgejo)

The Forgejo CI runner needs a `GH_PAT` Actions secret — a GitHub personal access token that can read public repositories (no scopes required) — so the `setup-just` and `setup-uv` actions can download their tools from github.com. A user- or organisation-level secret covers every repository of that owner; otherwise add it to this repository under **Settings → Actions → Secrets**.
{% if is_service %}
CD logs in to the container registry with the built-in `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `packages: write` permission, so it needs no additional secret.
{% endif %}{% endif %}

## Commands

```bash
{% if python == 'component' %}cd {{ component_dir }} && {% endif %}uv sync --frozen    # install / sync dependencies

just fix       # ruff format + ruff check --fix (auto-fixes, run before committing)
just lint      # format-check + ruff lint (fast, no typecheck)
just typecheck # pyright only
just test      # pytest with coverage
just static    # lint + typecheck (no tests)
just check     # full CI suite
```

`just check` composes atomic recipes (`just static test`), which in turn run:

```bash
ruff format --check
ruff check
pyright
pytest --cov --cov-report=term --cov-report=html
```

CI runs `just check` on every push and pull request.

## What CI checks

1. **Format** — ruff format verifies consistent formatting (no auto-fix in CI)
2. **Lint** — ruff with `select = ["ALL"]`; see `pyproject.toml` for the ignore list
3. **Typecheck** — pyright strict; no implicit `Any`, all public functions annotated
4. **Tests** — pytest with branch coverage; fails if coverage drops below 80%


## Pre-commit hooks
{% if hooks == 'none' %}
No pre-commit hooks are configured for this project.
{% else %}
Pre-commit hooks run automatically on `git commit`.

```bash
# Install hooks after cloning
pre-commit install

# Run manually against all files
pre-commit run --all-files
```

Each hook runs in an isolated virtualenv at a pinned version — more reproducible than calling tools directly. Hooks cover all file types, not just Python.

Active hooks:

| Hook | What it checks |
|------|---------------|
| `trailing-whitespace` | No trailing spaces (all files) |
| `end-of-file-fixer` | Files end with newline (all files) |
| `check-yaml` | Valid YAML syntax |
| `check-added-large-files` | No accidental large file commits |
| `detect-secrets` | No secrets or credentials committed |
| `no-commit-to-main` | Blocks commits directly on main/master |
{%- if hooks == 'python' %}
| `ruff` | Python lint (with auto-fix) |
| `ruff-format` | Python formatting |
| `pyright` | Python type checking |
{%- endif %}

### Secret detection

`detect-secrets` runs without a baseline file: every finding blocks the commit. Mark a false positive on its line:

```python
EXAMPLE_KEY = "AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE"  # pragma: allowlist secret
```

If a project accumulates false positives that cannot be annotated inline (generated files, fixtures full of fake keys), switch to a baseline: run `detect-secrets scan > .secrets.baseline`, commit the file, and add `args: ["--baseline", ".secrets.baseline"]` to the hook in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`.
{% endif %}

## Definition of done

A change is ready to merge when:

- [ ] `just check` (or equivalent) passes locally
- [ ] New behaviour has test coverage
- [ ] Any new architectural decision is recorded in `docs/adr/`
- [ ] `docs/` updated if the change affects documented behaviour
- [ ] CI is green on the PR
